This notice must be preserved in any distribution of that file;
tools/lint/check-determinism.sh fails the build if it is removed.

The reason for vendoring rather than calling the platform's libm is
recorded in SPEC section 11: Java's StrictMath is fdlibm, and a host libm
differs from it by up to one unit in the last place, which breaks Tier-A
parity. This code was taken from netlib, NOT from OpenJDK's StrictMath,
which is GPL+CE and incompatible with this repository's license.
